{"id": "EUVD-2026-104295", "enisaUuid": "199a91cd-5eca-3272-8fc8-c57e479eb7f7", "description": "rdesktop through 1.9.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in process_raw_bmpcache() in orders.c that allows malicious RDP servers to crash clients. Attackers can send a raw bitmap cache order declaring large width, height, and bpp values with a tiny payload, causing memcpy() to read past the receive buffer and crash the client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T13:55:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:52:31", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/rdesktop-bitmap-decompress-oob-read", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/pull/437", "https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/blob/v1.9.0/orders.c", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/rdesktop-through-1.9.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-process-raw-bmpcache"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f67q-4w46-jr64", "CVE-2026-112278"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.26, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2b1f9d84-8e18-32fa-86bb-0e202bdb0891", "product": {"name": "rdesktop", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0ecaf00c-81d1-313c-a6cf-75da20b2bf99", "vendor": {"name": "RDesktop"}}], "isExploited": false}